---
import Slide from "../../components/Slide.astro"
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro"
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import one_times from "../../img/iu000244_ddfs/1-times.png"

---
<Slide t1="React">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Front-end(*) framework for interaction
            and navigation in browser</li>
        <li class="fragment">Mix of markup and JavaScript (<code>JSX</code>)</li>
        <li class="fragment">Integrates into Astro (and VS Code)</li>
        <li class="fragment">Open Source</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="React Support">
    <ul>
        <li>Install with: <code><span class="text-red-500">npx</span> astro add react</code></li>
    </ul>
    
    <div class="text-sm-2">
        <CodeBlock lang="text" height="300px" lines="5,11">
            { "  " + `
  Astro will make the following changes to your config file:

 ╭ astro.config.mjs ─────────────────────────────╮
 │ // @ts-check                                  │
 │ import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';  │
 │                                               │
 │ import react from '@astrojs/react';           │
 │                                               │
 │ // https://astro.build/config                 │
 │ export default defineConfig({                 │
 │   integrations: [react()]                     │
 │ });                                           │
 ╰───────────────────────────────────────────────╯

✔ Continue? … yes`.trim()
            }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="React Support">
    <div class="text-sm-2">
        <CodeBlock lang="text" height="400px" lines="13-16">
            { "  " + `
  Astro will make the following changes to your tsconfig.json:

 ╭ tsconfig.json ──────────────────────────╮
 │ {                                       │
 │   "extends": "astro/tsconfigs/strict",  │
 │   "include": [                          │
 │     ".astro/types.d.ts",                │
 │     "**/*"                              │
 │   ],                                    │
 │   "exclude": [                          │
 │     "dist"                              │
 │   ],                                    │
 │   "compilerOptions": {                  │
 │     "jsx": "react-jsx",                 │
 │     "jsxImportSource": "react"          │
 │   }                                     │
 │ }                                       │
 ╰─────────────────────────────────────────╯

✔ Continue? … yes`.trim()
            }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>


<Slide t1="React Example">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Leaving Astro's static site features behind...</li>
        <li class="fragment">But: using it as a host and development environment</li>
        <li class="fragment">Astro can process <code>.jsx</code> files
            as if they were components</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Astro Page">
    <div class="text-sm-1">
        <CodeBlock lang="jsx" height="200px">
            { `
---
import ButtonPair from '../components/ButtonPair.jsx'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---
<Layout>
    <ButtonPair />
</Layout>`.trim()
            }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="React Component">
    <p>Single source file <code>ButtonPair.jsx</code></p>
    <div class="text-sm-2">
        <CodeBlock lang="jsx" height="250px">
            { `
import { useState } from 'react'

export default function ButtonPair() {
    return (
        <div>
            <h1>Counters that update separately</h1>
            <MyButton />
            <MyButton />
        </div>
    )
}
`.trim() }
        </CodeBlock>

        <CodeBlock lang="jsx" height="250px">
            { `
function MyButton() {
    const [count, setCount] = useState(0)
  
    function handleClick() {
        setCount(count + 1)
    }
  
    return (
        <button onClick={handleClick}>
            Clicked {count} times
        </button>
    )
}
    `.trim() }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>

    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">Does this actually work?</li>
        <li class="fragment">Hint: no &#x1F616;</li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Astro: Hydration">
    <ul>
        <li class="fragment">React will run server-side: and
            this is what Astro is doing here</li>
        <li class="fragment">We need to <em>hydrate</em> the component
            so that it is passed to the client (browser)</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="fragment text-sm-1">
        <CodeBlock lang="jsx" height="150px">
            { `
<Layout>
    <ButtonPair client:only />
</Layout>`.trim()
            }
        </CodeBlock>
    </div>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Exercises">
    <ul>
        <li>Can you extend <code>MyButton</code> so that it can also count down?</li>
        <li>How about a reset to zero function?</li>
        <li>As this gets more visually complicated: perhaps add some styling
            (colour, spacing) and additional text hints
        </li>
    </ul>
</Slide>

<Slide t2="Exercise (Trickier?)">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-20">
        <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
            <Image
                src={ one_times }
                alt="iPhone Message"
                height="300"
                width="450" />
        </div>

        <div>
            <ul>
                <li class="fragment">Don't be this programmer</li>
                <li class="fragment">What is wrong with this content?</li>
                <li class="fragment">How do we fix it in our button example?
                    (<code>Clicked 0 times </code> /
                    <code>1 <span class="text-red-500">time</span></code> /
                    <code>2 times</code> etc.)</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</Slide>
